{"contract":{"core_question":"What changed between audit runs of a spec, and how has the audit trajectory evolved over time?","entities":[{"name":"formatRelativeTime utility","type":"function","path":"dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.ts","function":"formatRelativeTime","created_by_task":"1","key_fields":["converts ISO timestamp to relative string","handles edge cases: future, empty, boundary values","returns just now, Nm ago, Nh ago, Nd ago, or short date"]},{"name":"issueKey utility","type":"function","path":"dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.ts","function":"issueKey","created_by_task":"1","key_fields":["composite key from ruleId + section","used for matching issues across audit runs"]},{"name":"computeComparison utility","type":"function","path":"dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.ts","function":"computeComparison","created_by_task":"2","key_fields":["accepts two SpeedAuditResult objects","returns removed unchanged added issue groups","uses issueKey for matching"]},{"name":"getPersistentIssues utility","type":"function","path":"dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.ts","function":"getPersistentIssues","created_by_task":"2","key_fields":["accepts latest and previous audit","returns Set of issueKeys present in both"]},{"name":"useAuditHistory hook","type":"function","path":"dashboard/frontend/components/editor/use-audit-history.ts","function":"useAuditHistory","created_by_task":"3","key_fields":["selectedRunIndex state with clamping","compareIndices state with validation","selectRun shiftSelectRun exitComparison resetToLatest actions","Escape key handler with two-level exit"]},{"name":"audit-history-utils test file","type":"file","path":"dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.test.ts","created_by_task":"4","key_fields":["formatRelativeTime edge cases","issueKey uniqueness","computeComparison correctness","getPersistentIssues correctness"]},{"name":"use-audit-history test file","type":"file","path":"dashboard/frontend/components/editor/use-audit-history.test.ts","created_by_task":"5","key_fields":["selectedRunIndex clamping","compareIndices validation","escape key two-level exit","shift-click state transitions"]}],"relationships":[],"core_queries":[{"description":"Format an audit timestamp as a human-readable relative time string","traversal":"audit.ranAt -> formatRelativeTime -> relative string","answers":"When did this audit run?"},{"description":"Compare two audit runs to categorize findings as added, removed, or unchanged","traversal":"olderAudit.issues + newerAudit.issues -> computeComparison -> removed unchanged added","answers":"What changed between two audit runs?"},{"description":"Identify persistent issues that survived across consecutive audit runs","traversal":"latestAudit.issues + previousAudit.issues -> getPersistentIssues -> Set of issueKeys","answers":"Which issues keep coming back across audit iterations?"},{"description":"Manage run selection and comparison state with validation and clamping","traversal":"user interaction -> useAuditHistory -> selectedRunIndex compareIndices actions","answers":"Which audit run is the user currently viewing or comparing?"}]},"tasks":[{"id":"1","title":"Create formatRelativeTime and issueKey utility functions","description":"Create `dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.ts` with two pure utility functions.\n\n**`formatRelativeTime(isoString: string): string`**\nConverts an ISO 8601 timestamp to a human-readable relative time string:\n- Empty/invalid input returns 'unknown'\n- < 60 seconds ago returns 'just now'\n- < 60 minutes ago returns 'Nm ago' (e.g. '5m ago')\n- < 24 hours ago returns 'Nh ago' (e.g. '3h ago')\n- < 7 days ago returns 'Nd ago' (e.g. '2d ago')\n- >= 7 days ago returns short date 'Mar 15' using Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' })\n\nCompute the diff as `Date.now() - new Date(isoString).getTime()`. Check `isNaN` on the parsed date for invalid input.\n\n**`issueKey(issue: AuditIssue): string`**\nProduces a composite string key for matching issues across runs. Format: `${section}::${identifier}` where identifier is `ruleId` if available, otherwise first 80 chars of `message`. Import the `AuditIssue` type from the existing codebase. Check IntelPanel.tsx or the GraphQL types directory for the type definition. If `AuditIssue` does not have a `ruleId` field, use `section + '::' + message.slice(0, 80)`.\n\nExport both functions as named exports. Also export a `ComparisonResult` interface placeholder (just the type, implementation in task 2): `{ removed: AuditIssue[], unchanged: AuditIssue[], added: AuditIssue[] }`.","files_touched":["dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.ts"],"depends_on":[],"agent_model":"sonnet","acceptance_criteria":"- formatRelativeTime('') returns 'unknown' [verify: test]\n- formatRelativeTime with invalid date string returns 'unknown' [verify: test]\n- formatRelativeTime with timestamp 30s ago returns 'just now' [verify: test]\n- formatRelativeTime with timestamp 5min ago returns '5m ago' [verify: test]\n- formatRelativeTime with timestamp 3h ago returns '3h ago' [verify: test]\n- formatRelativeTime with timestamp 2d ago returns '2d ago' [verify: test]\n- formatRelativeTime with timestamp 10d ago returns short date like 'Mar 15' [verify: test]\n- issueKey produces different keys for issues with same section but different messages [verify: test]\n- issueKey produces identical keys for the same issue across two audit runs [verify: test]\n- File exports formatRelativeTime, issueKey, and ComparisonResult as named exports [verify: lint]"},{"id":"2","title":"Create computeComparison and getPersistentIssues functions","description":"Add to `dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.ts` two functions that build on `issueKey`.\n\n**`computeComparison(olderAudit: SpeedAuditResult, newerAudit: SpeedAuditResult): ComparisonResult`**\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build `Map<string, AuditIssue>` from olderAudit.issues using issueKey as key.\n2. Build `Map<string, AuditIssue>` from newerAudit.issues using issueKey as key.\n3. removed = iterate older map, collect entries whose key is absent from newer map.\n4. added = iterate newer map, collect entries whose key is absent from older map.\n5. unchanged = iterate newer map, collect entries whose key exists in older map.\nReturn `{ removed, unchanged, added }`.\n\n**`getPersistentIssues(latestAudit: SpeedAuditResult, previousAudit: SpeedAuditResult | null): Set<string>`**\nIf previousAudit is null, return empty Set. Otherwise build Sets of issueKeys from each audit's issues array. Return the intersection (keys present in both). \n\nImport SpeedAuditResult from the existing type definitions. Look in IntelPanel.tsx or the GraphQL types for the existing interface. The type has at minimum: `{ status: string, issues: AuditIssue[], sizing: object | null, ranAt: string }`.","files_touched":["dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.ts"],"depends_on":["1"],"agent_model":"sonnet","acceptance_criteria":"- computeComparison with identical audits returns all issues in unchanged, empty removed and added [verify: test]\n- computeComparison with completely different audits returns all in removed and added, empty unchanged [verify: test]\n- computeComparison with mixed changes correctly categorizes each issue [verify: test]\n- computeComparison with both audits having empty issues arrays returns all groups empty [verify: test]\n- getPersistentIssues returns empty Set when previousAudit is null [verify: test]\n- getPersistentIssues returns correct issueKey strings for issues present in both audits [verify: test]\n- getPersistentIssues returns empty Set when no issues overlap [verify: test]"},{"id":"3","title":"Create useAuditHistory state management hook","description":"Create `dashboard/frontend/components/editor/use-audit-history.ts` with a custom React hook that manages all audit history selection state.\n\n**`useAuditHistory(auditCount: number)`** returns `AuditHistoryState`.\n\nState variables:\n- `selectedRunIndex: number` (useState, init 0)\n- `compareIndices: [number, number] | null` (useState, init null)\n\nDerived:\n- `isComparing: boolean` = compareIndices !== null\n\nActions (wrap each in useCallback with appropriate deps):\n- `selectRun(index: number)`: clamp index to [0, auditCount-1]. If index === current selectedRunIndex, reset to 0 (toggle off). Otherwise set selectedRunIndex to clamped index. Always clear compareIndices.\n- `shiftSelectRun(index: number)`: if auditCount < 2, return (no-op). Clamp index. If compareIndices is null, create tuple from [selectedRunIndex, index] sorted ascending (lower index = newer run). If the two indices are equal, return (can't compare run with itself). Set compareIndices, clear selectedRunIndex to 0. If compareIndices is already set and index matches one existing entry, clear compareIndices (cancel comparison). If index is new, replace the higher-numbered (older) entry in the tuple.\n- `exitComparison()`: set compareIndices to null, set selectedRunIndex to 0.\n- `resetToLatest()`: set compareIndices to null, set selectedRunIndex to 0.\n\nEffects:\n- Clamping effect: useEffect watching auditCount. If selectedRunIndex >= auditCount, set to Math.max(0, auditCount - 1). If compareIndices has any index >= auditCount, clear compareIndices.\n- Escape handler: useEffect adding keydown listener on document. On Escape: if isComparing, call exitComparison. Else if selectedRunIndex !== 0, call resetToLatest. Cleanup removes listener.\n\nExport the `AuditHistoryState` interface and the hook as default export.","files_touched":["dashboard/frontend/components/editor/use-audit-history.ts"],"depends_on":[],"agent_model":"sonnet","acceptance_criteria":"- Initial state: selectedRunIndex=0, compareIndices=null, isComparing=false [verify: test]\n- selectRun(1) sets selectedRunIndex to 1 [verify: test]\n- selectRun with same index toggles back to 0 [verify: test]\n- selectRun(5) with auditCount=3 clamps to 2 [verify: test]\n- selectRun clears any active compareIndices [verify: test]\n- shiftSelectRun is no-op when auditCount < 2 [verify: test]\n- shiftSelectRun with two different valid indices enters comparison mode [verify: test]\n- shiftSelectRun on existing compare index cancels comparison [verify: test]\n- Escape exits comparison mode on first press, deselects on second [verify: test]\n- selectedRunIndex auto-clamps when auditCount shrinks [verify: test]\n- compareIndices cleared when auditCount makes indices invalid [verify: test]\n- AuditHistoryState type is exported [verify: lint]"},{"id":"4","title":"Unit tests for audit history utility functions","description":"Create `dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.test.ts` with comprehensive vitest unit tests.\n\nUse `vi.useFakeTimers()` and `vi.setSystemTime()` to control Date.now() for formatRelativeTime tests. Create a helper `isoAgo(ms: number)` that returns `new Date(Date.now() - ms).toISOString()`.\n\n**describe('formatRelativeTime')**\n- it('returns unknown for empty string')\n- it('returns unknown for invalid date')\n- it('returns just now for 0 seconds ago')\n- it('returns just now for 30 seconds ago')\n- it('returns just now for 59 seconds ago')\n- it('returns 1m ago at 60 second boundary')\n- it('returns 45m ago for 45 minutes')\n- it('returns 1h ago at 60 minute boundary')\n- it('returns 23h ago for 23 hours')\n- it('returns 1d ago at 24 hour boundary')\n- it('returns 6d ago for 6 days')\n- it('returns short date at 7 day boundary')\n- it('returns short date for 30 days ago')\n- it('handles future timestamps gracefully')\n\n**describe('issueKey')**\n- it('generates key from section and ruleId')\n- it('falls back to message truncation without ruleId')\n- it('produces different keys for different messages in same section')\n- it('produces same key for identical issues')\n- it('handles empty section gracefully')\n\n**describe('computeComparison')**\n- it('returns empty groups for empty audits')\n- it('puts all issues in unchanged for identical audits')\n- it('puts issues in removed and added for completely different audits')\n- it('correctly categorizes mixed changes')\n- it('treats issue moved to different section as removed + added')\n\n**describe('getPersistentIssues')**\n- it('returns empty set for null previous')\n- it('returns empty set for no overlap')\n- it('returns all keys for full overlap')\n- it('returns only shared keys for partial overlap')\n\nConstruct mock SpeedAuditResult objects inline with minimal required fields.","files_touched":["dashboard/frontend/components/editor/audit-history-utils.test.ts"],"depends_on":["2"],"agent_model":"sonnet","acceptance_criteria":"- All formatRelativeTime boundary and edge case tests pass [verify: test]\n- All issueKey uniqueness and identity tests pass [verify: test]\n- All computeComparison categorization tests pass [verify: test]\n- All getPersistentIssues intersection tests pass [verify: test]\n- Tests use vitest describe/it/expect and vi.useFakeTimers [verify: lint]\n- No import errors from audit-history-utils.ts [verify: lint]"},{"id":"5","title":"Unit tests for useAuditHistory hook","description":"Create `dashboard/frontend/components/editor/use-audit-history.test.ts` with hook tests.\n\nUse `renderHook` and `act` from `@testing-library/react`. Use `fireEvent.keyDown(document, { key: 'Escape' })` for keyboard tests.\n\n**describe('useAuditHistory')**\n\n**describe('initial state')**\n- it('starts with selectedRunIndex=0, compareIndices=null, isComparing=false')\n\n**describe('selectRun')**\n- it('sets selectedRunIndex to given index')\n- it('toggles back to 0 when selecting current index')\n- it('clamps to auditCount-1 when index exceeds bounds')\n- it('clears compareIndices when selecting a run')\n\n**describe('shiftSelectRun')**\n- it('is no-op when auditCount is 1')\n- it('enters comparison mode with sorted indices')\n- it('cancels comparison when clicking existing compare index')\n- it('replaces older index when third dot shift-clicked')\n- it('prevents comparing a run with itself')\n\n**describe('escape key')**\n- it('exits comparison mode on first Escape')\n- it('deselects run on Escape when not comparing')\n- it('is no-op at default state')\n- it('handles two rapid Escape presses correctly')\n\n**describe('clamping')**\n- it('clamps selectedRunIndex when auditCount decreases')\n- it('clears compareIndices when auditCount makes indices invalid')\n- it('handles auditCount going to 0')\n\nFor rerender tests (clamping), use `renderHook` with `initialProps` and call `rerender({ auditCount: newValue })`.","files_touched":["dashboard/frontend/components/editor/use-audit-history.test.ts"],"depends_on":["3"],"agent_model":"sonnet","acceptance_criteria":"- All selectRun state transition tests pass [verify: test]\n- All shiftSelectRun comparison mode entry/exit tests pass [verify: test]\n- Escape key two-level exit tests pass [verify: test]\n- Index clamping on auditCount decrease tests pass [verify: test]\n- Self-comparison prevention test passes [verify: test]\n- Tests use renderHook and act from @testing-library/react [verify: lint]\n- Hook imported correctly from use-audit-history.ts [verify: lint]"}],"validation":[{"severity":"warning","issue":"Product spec AH3 (net issue count trend across runs in verdict strip) has no explicit function in the tech spec. The comparison mode shows delta between two selected runs, but AH3 asks for a visible trend across all runs without entering comparison mode.","product_requirement":"AH3: As a spec author, I want to see a net issue count trend across runs","recommendation":"Phase 2 should include a task for rendering issue counts alongside verdict dots in the verdict strip. The design spec's Verdict counts typography entry at 10px mono suggests this is intended."},{"severity":"warning","issue":"Tech spec says issueKey uses section + message[:80]. Design spec says matching uses ruleId + section. Inconsistent keying strategies.","product_requirement":"AH2/AH4: Comparison and persistent issue detection depend on correct issue matching","recommendation":"Task 1 instructs the developer to prefer ruleId + section when ruleId exists, falling back to message truncation. Developer should inspect AuditIssue type for actual available fields."},{"severity":"note","issue":"Arrow key navigation between dots is deferred to Phase 2 since it requires rendered button elements with roving tabindex.","product_requirement":"In Scope: Keyboard navigation (Escape to exit, arrow keys between dots)","recommendation":"Phase 2 tasks should implement roving tabindex on verdict strip buttons. Phase 1 handles only Escape."},{"severity":"note","issue":"Product spec success criterion 'Works with both audit-*.json and plan-audit-*.json files' depends on the backend recentAudits query behavior, not frontend logic.","product_requirement":"Works with both audit-*.json and plan-audit-*.json files","recommendation":"Verify in Phase 2 integration that recentAudits returns both file types. No Phase 1 action needed since tech spec confirms existing query handles this."}]}
